This is incorrect.  If there is a 1/4000 chance of finding a wand of wishing
on the first level (and no chance of finding more than one), then the prob-
ability of finding exactly one WOW on the first level in the first 4000 games
is (3999/4000)^3999, which is about .37, or 37%. This is computed by consider-
ing that there are 4000 ways this could happen: a wand found on the 1st try
and never another,  a wand found on the second try and never another, etc.
Each of these outcomes has probability 1/4000*(3999/4000)^3999, and there
are 4000 different outcomes, so multiply by 4000 to get the answer.

